From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: encomjp <46200173+encomjp@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat Aug 30 2026 23:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] hwmon: yogafan: add DMI quirk for LOQ 15AHP10 (83JG / R8CN)

LOQ 15AHP10 (machine type 83JG, BIOS prefix R8CN) ships with an
ITE IT5508 EC whose tachometer is locked behind the yogafan ACPI
interface.  lenovo_wmi_other binds but every fanN_input reads 0 RPM,
and the WMI3 GetFanSpeed / ACPI temp paths return -5 (AE_ERROR).
The real RPM lives in the EC at 0xFE/0xFF and is exposed only through
yogafan's ACPI methods \_SB.PCI0.LPC0.EC0.FANS (fan1, 16-bit LE) and
\_SB.PCI0.LPC0.EC0.FA2S (fan2, 16-bit LE).  Without an explicit DMI
quirk the driver falls back to the generic 8-bit FAN0 path and reports
0 RPM on idle *and* under load; fleet telemetry (2327 reports,
2026-08-29 triage) shows fan_rpms_readable failing on 100% of LOQ
reports.

Add a DMI quirk that matches LENOVO 83JG (and the R8CN BIOS family)
to the existing 2-fan 16-bit configuration, so the tachometer is
readable from boot even at 0 RPM idle (yogafan becomes the primary
fan hwmon).  The companion userspace change (legion-tool 0.2.5:
fans::needs_yogafan_setup / ensure_yogafan_loaded, DeepReport
yogafan_loaded + fan_detail, 83JG/R8CN hard-profile in models.rs)
prefers yogafan whenever WMI is all-zero and auto-modprobes the
module via /etc/modules-load.d/legion-yogafan.conf.

Tested on:  LOQ 15AHP10 83JG R8CN28WW, kernel 7.2.2-1-cachyos-bore
             (yogafan intree, 6.14+ / 7.x).  After the quirk:
               /sys/class/hwmon/hwmonN/name = yogafan
               fan1_input/fan2_input report live RPM (16-bit, 500..5500)
               legion-tool diagnostics: yogafan_loaded=true,
                 fan_detail carries yogafan fan1_*/fan2_* attrs,
                 device profile matched 83JG/R8CN (LOQ Gen 10, 2 fans)

References: LenovoLegionLinux #384/#453/#467, kernel yogafan.c,
            research/EC-REGISTER-MAP.md, telemetry-triage/TRIAGE-2026-08-29.md

Signed-off-by: encomjp <46200173+encomjp@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/hwmon/yogafan.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/hwmon/yogafan.c b/drivers/hwmon/yogafan.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/drivers/hwmon/yogafan.c
+++ b/drivers/hwmon/yogafan.c
@@ -45,6 +45,21 @@ static const struct dmi_system_id yogafan_quirks[] = {
 		.ident = "IdeaPad Gaming 3",
 		.matches = {
 			DMI_MATCH(DMI_SYS_VENDOR, "LENOVO"),
 			DMI_MATCH(DMI_PRODUCT_FAMILY, "IdeaPad"),
 		},
 		.driver_data = &ideapad_8bit_fan0_cfg,
 	},
+	{
+		.ident = "LOQ 15AHP10 (83JG)",
+		.matches = {
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_SYS_VENDOR, "LENOVO"),
+			/* product_name is the 4-char machine type (83JG); BIOS prefix is R8CN */
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_PRODUCT_NAME, "83JG"),
+		},
+		.driver_data = &yogafan_2fan_16bit_cfg,
+	},
+	{
+		.ident = "LOQ 15AHP10 (R8CN BIOS)",
+		.matches = {
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_SYS_VENDOR, "LENOVO"),
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_BIOS_VERSION, "R8CN"),
+		},
+		.driver_data = &yogafan_2fan_16bit_cfg,
+	},
 	{ }
 };
